WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.700
The verdict is in: Mortal Kombat is a pretty
fun movie.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:10.420
Critics and fans alike are praising it for
not taking itself or its story too seriously,

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:16.080
but even in that spirit, some aspects of its
story suffer from plot holes that can't easily

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.080
be brushed aside.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:25.320
"Mortal Kombat" begins at a dire moment: Outworld
will invade if Earthrealm loses one more tournament.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:31.320
At the same time, an ancient prophecy states
that Earthrealm will see new champions arise

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.859
"by the rise of Hanzo Hasashi's blood."

00:00:34.859 --> 00:00:41.839
With this looming prophecy about Hanzo Hasashi's
bloodline, Outworld sorcerer Shang Tsung wants

00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:46.800
to eliminate the remainder of Earthrealm's
warriors before the tournament so it isn't

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.479
possible for Earthrealm to win.

00:00:49.479 --> 00:00:53.449
The only problem with that plan is that none
of it makes sense.

00:00:53.449 --> 00:00:58.690
Shang Tsung's conversation with Mileena about
the plan is pretty telling — she worries

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:04.129
that Raiden may discover their breakage of
"rules set in stone by the Elder Gods," and

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:09.150
he responds that they didn't "win nine straight
tournaments by following the rules."

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:14.240
Later, when he invades Lord Raiden's temple
with Sub-Zero and Mileena, he is confronted

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:20.070
by Raiden, who notes that "It is forbidden
to claim victory until the tournament begins."

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:25.729
Shang Tsung replies with the assertion that
the other Gods will be, quote, "too lazy"

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:27.049
to stop him.

00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:29.299
There are problems with this logic.

00:01:29.299 --> 00:01:35.840
First, Shang Tsung acknowledges they've managed
to cheat enough to win nine times in a row

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.070
without thus far getting caught.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:40.710
Why doubt their ability to do so now?

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:46.440
On the other hand, killing Earthrealm warriors
outside Mortal Kombat won't win the right

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.420
to invade Earthrealm.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:56.789
Basically, Shang Tsung inexplicably takes
a much more complicated, brazen path towards

00:01:56.789 --> 00:02:00.280
cheating than just fighting in the tournament
like he had before.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.640
It's not like his winning record needs the
help.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.710
And if he's going to cheat anyway, why now?

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:10.930
Why not earlier, between tournaments when
Earth's marked defenders would be teenagers,

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:11.930
or even younger?

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.190
None of it quite adds up.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:19.170
Liu Kang says that his charge is to gather
all the champions of Earth.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.720
The trouble is that he's extremely bad at
his job.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:28.580
We become aware through conversations between
Sonya and Cole that she and Jax had long been

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.510
aware of a number of marked champions.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:37.200
We're also told that many of those champions
are dead, since Liu Kang notes "there are

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.010
not many of us with the markings left."

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:45.570
The series of events that brings our group
of champions together is due to Sub-Zero finding

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:52.700
Cole first, bringing him, Jax, and Sonya together
-- but not without first almost killing Jax

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.030
and Cole.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:03:00.380
Meanwhile Cole, Sonya, and Kano make their
way towards the temple of Lord Raiden because

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:06.150
Sonya just happens to be part of a group who
has connected all these dots, and Kano happens

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.010
to know the location of Lord Raiden's temple.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:14.950
When they get there — no thanks to Liu Kang
— he seems surprised to see them, saying,

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.010
"At last!

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:19.740
Finally, you have come to seek out Raiden's
temple."

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:25.130
Despite the apparent urgency of needing to
gather all the champions of Earth for an all-important

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:31.120
Tournament that's about a month away, Liu
Kang was seemingly content to just sit around

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.220
and wait on the off chance it all worked out.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:39.660
For someone charged with bringing together
Earthrealm's champions, at no point did Liu

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.470
Kang find, bring, or train any champions.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:48.460
Meanwhile, other marked champions seem to
be dying all the time, and we have no evidence

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.820
he intervened at any point to gather or protect
them.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:57.930
The entire reason it all worked out is because
Cole was saved by Jax, shepherded by the unmarked

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:04.280
Sonya, and guided by the untrustworthy Kano
(who isn't even supposed to have the mark).

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:09.900
So If Liu Kang really is supposed to be gathering
the heroes of Earthrealm, he's absolutely

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.740
and completely terrible at it.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:19.000
When Sonya Blade, Cole Young, and Kano arrive
at Lord Raiden's temple, Liu Kang and Kung

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.940
Lao immediately take to training them.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.460
Cole, Kano, and Jax each have the dragon mark.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:30.710
With Jax recovering from his minor arm injury,
the more experienced warriors take to training

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.440
Cole and Kano.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:39.090
The issue: Kano from the get-go is a rough,
disrespectful, power-hungry narcissist with

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.500
a criminal background.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:46.030
They train him with the rest of the warriors
until they discover his arcana — and he

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:52.040
easily becomes persuaded by Shang Tsung's
forces with the promise of more power.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:57.850
He compromises the defenses of Lord Raiden's
temple, and engages the heroes in combat with

00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:00.570
the arcana they helped him attain.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:05.610
Here's the complication with training anyone
who enters the temple: warriors can absolutely

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:11.139
change sides and betray Earthrealm with their
powers, helping Outworld's conquest of the

00:05:11.139 --> 00:05:12.300
realm.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:16.810
With a small number of fighters, losing one
to the other side is a pretty big change in

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:18.220
the balance of forces.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:23.960
Why, then, train literally anyone as soon
as they enter, especially if they seem like

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:24.960
a shady character?

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:30.760
When Sonya Blade meets Cole, the first thing
she wants to know is if he has the dragon

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.760
mark.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:37.370
When she, Cole, and Kano arrive at Lord Raiden's
temple, they're reminded repeatedly how important

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.770
the marking is.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:44.480
Raiden reinforces to Cole how without his
arcana — which one needs the Mark to get

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.350
— he's really of no use to the fight.

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:52.840
Liu Kang repeatedly reiterates how you're
a liability without being chosen and having

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.190
your Arcana.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:06:00.040
Mileena even refuses to kill Sonya because,
without the mark, she has no value in the

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.760
scheme of the struggle between realms.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.940
With all this in mind: why is Sonya even there?

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:10.661
She's a great character and a pivotal part
of the plot but, in terms of the story, it

00:06:10.661 --> 00:06:12.400
doesn't make sense.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:17.970
She's let into Raiden's temple, and though
Kung Lao does forbid her from actively training

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:23.410
with the others, she's still basically involved
with the entirety of the conflict with Shang

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:24.590
Tsung.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:29.730
She's even pulled by Raiden into his void
to prepare for the team's final battle plan,

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:35.400
which happens before she duels Kano, kills
him, and finally gains the mark.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:40.880
Given the rules that are continually reinforced,
and the strict messaging that people without

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:46.850
arcana are a liability, Sonya's deep involvement
with Raiden's group of warriors makes no sense.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:54.410
When Cole meets Sonya, they have one strange
guest tied to a chair: Kano.

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:59.510
Sonya explains that he had just been caught
after killing the fate-chosen champion they'd

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:03.310
previously been looking for, thus securing
a mark for himself.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:08.750
At this point, Jax had already gained a dragon
mark, but Sonya had not.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:13.960
Regardless, Sonya knows through her research
the importance of the marks for signifying

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:19.440
Earth's champion defenders in the Mortal Kombat
tournament, and that the tournament is pivotal

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:21.040
in protecting Earthrealm.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:26.940
She knows the stakes are high, that not having
a mark impedes her ability to fight for Earth.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:32.110
And she also knows that killing a mark-bearer
transfers the mark to the victor.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:36.910
Sonya had all this knowledge while maintaining
the upper hand on a criminal scumbag like

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:40.230
Kano who had just killed a champion of Earth.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:46.110
Also, at this point, Sonya isn't aware that
he knows the location of Lord Raiden's temple.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:51.139
There is no clear reason to keep him around
as a prisoner who killed one of Earth's champions,

00:07:51.139 --> 00:07:55.880
especially when the stakes are so high and
he has the mark that would allow her to protect

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:57.860
the Earth instead of him.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:02.930
Heroes are often written to avoid killing
out of some kind of personal moral code, but

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:08.430
this is "Mortal Kombat," and Sonya's background
as a soldier is a testament to her willingness

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.560
to kill threats when necessary.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:16.610
With all of this in mind, capturing Kano rather
than taking his mark was an inexplicable choice

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.540
for her character to make.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:23.350
Moreover, had she killed him, Earth would
have had one more champion against the apocalypse

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.449
— and one less enemy of humanity.

00:08:26.449 --> 00:08:32.270
The new "Mortal Kombat" film introduces a
further innovation to the "MK" universe, beyond

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:35.209
the creation of Cole Young: arcana.

00:08:35.209 --> 00:08:41.169
The dragon markings mean you're a chosen champion,
and chosen champions spend the movie struggling

00:08:41.169 --> 00:08:46.290
to activate their arcana: in other words,
their unique power.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:52.910
Arcana is unique to the individual — it
can be Kano's laser eye, Liu Kang's fire powers,

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:56.970
Cole's brass armor and weapons, or something
else entirely.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:01.380
It's unpredictable, powerful ... and woefully
unclear.

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:07.079
Liu Kang informs Kano, Cole, and Sonya of
the importance of having a marking and finding

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:09.339
your personal arcana.

00:09:09.339 --> 00:09:14.430
As he explains to everyone, "If you fail to
discover your inner power, you will never

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:16.180
defeat your opponent."

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:21.800
He even directly addresses a comment to Sonya
-- but it's terribly unclear why he's even

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:26.420
talking to Sonya because she can't discover
her power and doesn't have a mark.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:32.259
Later, Liu Kang clarifies that the fighters'
inner power comes from the arcana, and that

00:09:32.259 --> 00:09:35.259
the point of their training is to unlock that
power.

00:09:35.259 --> 00:09:37.029
How does that work?

00:09:37.029 --> 00:09:40.749
Well, there's a variety of competing explanations.

00:09:40.749 --> 00:09:44.760
He first explains that they'll discover their
arcana by training in the fight pit.

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:50.960
Later, he clarifies that the arcana's activation
must come from their soul, and whatever it

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:53.100
is that drives them.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:58.760
Later still, he says that "Pain is the ultimate
catalyst" towards finding the arcana.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:04.620
This all effectively means that the warriors'
arcanas all manifest in random and very individual

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:08.510
ways, making it seem like a pointless thing
to train for.

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:15.209
Liu Kang seems entirely convinced that arcana
manifests from pain in the process of training

00:10:15.209 --> 00:10:20.509
in the pits, but that's not what activates
arcana for almost any character.

00:10:20.509 --> 00:10:23.819
Cole's emerges from his daughter's strength
bracelet.

00:10:23.819 --> 00:10:27.779
If she didn't make that, would his arcana
be entirely different?

00:10:27.779 --> 00:10:33.220
Furthermore, the relationship between getting
the mark and getting the arcana is seemingly

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:34.220
random.

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:40.269
Liu Kang kills a child trafficker on assignment
and gets his arcana immediately in the process.

00:10:40.269 --> 00:10:43.660
Sonya gets her mark and her arcana by killing
Kano.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:47.540
Kano got his from his ego being wounded.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:53.009
Cole is born with his mark and no fights nor
dangers activate his arcana until his family

00:10:53.009 --> 00:10:54.360
is in danger.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:59.259
Jax kills someone to get his mark ... and
doesn't get arcana until his arms are ripped

00:10:59.259 --> 00:11:04.110
off, he's supernaturally given new arms, and
Sonya's endangered.

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:09.069
Why is the emergence so randomly timed, and
the form so arbitrary?

00:11:09.069 --> 00:11:12.440
And why does Liu Kang think it's related to
fighting when it isn't?

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:18.360
As far as protectors of Earthrealm go, Raiden
is quite inconsistent.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:25.499
In Hanzo Hasashi's life, Raiden doesn't intervene
when Bi-Han kills him, and he allows the assassin

00:11:25.499 --> 00:11:26.910
to kill much of his family.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:32.939
But then he shows up to collect Hanzo's infant
daughter to protect his lineage, and keeps

00:11:32.939 --> 00:11:38.630
his kunai to facilitate Scorpion's later emergence
when Earthrealm needed it most.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:43.709
Basically, Raiden continually asserts he's
"not allowed to intervene," despite the fact

00:11:43.709 --> 00:11:45.589
that he keeps intervening anyway.

00:11:45.589 --> 00:11:51.209
The biggest inconsistency, however, is when
Shang Tsung and his fighters arrive in Raiden's

00:11:51.209 --> 00:11:56.989
temple in force, and Raiden essentially pauses
the fight to pull the Earthrealm defenders

00:11:56.989 --> 00:11:59.389
into the void between realms.

00:11:59.389 --> 00:12:00.970
Some of them, anyway.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:06.959
Due to Sub-Zero and Shang Tsung's counterattacks,
he doesn't manage to immediately teleport

00:12:06.959 --> 00:12:14.430
Cole or Kung Lao, the latter of whom gets
his soul gruesomely consumed by Shang Tsung.

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:18.459
Immediately afterwards, Liu Kang and Cole
are teleported away.

00:12:18.459 --> 00:12:24.499
Jax asks Raiden why he couldn't save him,
to which Raiden replies, "Elder Gods are forbidden

00:12:24.499 --> 00:12:30.800
from engaging in one realm's war against another
... it is my job to protect Earthrealm but

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.489
I cannot save every soul within it."

00:12:33.489 --> 00:12:38.100
But he literally did just engage in the war
by teleporting people away to regroup, in

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:42.569
a tide-turning move that proves to be extremely
successful.

00:12:42.569 --> 00:12:47.860
Raiden intervened so much that he managed
to save every other Earthrealm champion.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:53.819
He even pulls Kung Lao's Razor-Rimmed Hat
into the teleportation lightning at the last

00:12:53.819 --> 00:12:56.350
second, just not the warrior himself.

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:58.279
Poor guy.

00:12:58.279 --> 00:13:00.220
"Flawless victory."

